&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain solutions that power data deletion and data access, ensuring they remain effective in a dynamic landscape of global regulations and user expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of new privacy features, tools, and scalable solutions to optimize the work of the Privacy Engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams, including Engineering, Product, Data, and Legal to ensure product goals align with Discord’s Privacy Principles and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for privacy-preserving solutions and identify new opportunities to promote our privacy posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a clear vision and roadmap for privacy technology at Discord that is aligned with and supports the efforts and goals of Discord’s cross-functional Privacy organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Privacy incident response efforts, including mitigating situations that may pose a risk to our Privacy Principles, and providing assistance in incident response efforts outside of the privacy domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for user privacy and data protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of work experience in Privacy or Security engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in at least one general purpose programming language (e.g. Python, Rust, Go).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience working in cloud-based environments (we use Google Cloud).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with concepts and practices such as threat modeling, privacy by design, privacy enhancing technologies, and auditing access to data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with privacy concerns that apply in an industry setting, including consent, deletion, and retention, and a basic understanding of regulations such as GDPR or CCPA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
